# Copy to `.env` (gitignored). LOCAL DEV TOGGLE ONLY.
#
# This file never decides what a build or an OTA ships: every EAS build profile
# and `ota:export` pin the value themselves, so what you set here only affects
# `expo start` on your own machine.
#
# Two states, nothing else:
#   mock → serve the local axios-adapter fixtures (src/api/mocks), no network
#   real → hit the live backend (URL is hardcoded in src/api/client.ts)
#
# Only the literal string `mock` enables fixtures; any other value means real.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_MODE=real

# NEVER put a secret in this file — it is a credential at rest in the working
# tree, one `git add -f` away from permanent exposure. (A secret here WOULD
# load: `@expo/env` assigns every non-denylisted key, not just EXPO_PUBLIC_*.
# The prefix governs bundle INLINING, not loading — so never prefix a secret
# with EXPO_PUBLIC_ either; those ship inside the app.)
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN lives in `eas env` at `sensitive` visibility.
